-- title:
--   Spreading of the Γ̃-orbit relation at level ℓ
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic and coefficient data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$ and a nonzero natural number $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$, with $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic filtration, $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi)) = r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$ (so $\mathcal O$ is absolutely unramified with residue field of cardinality $r$), together with a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. A characteristic-zero domain $Onr$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`) and every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`); an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$ of $Onr$ with $Fr(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ (`hFr`). Thus $Onr$ plays the role of the ring of integers of the completed maximal unramified extension of $\mathcal O$ and $Fr$ of its Frobenius. Finally a homomorphism $v\det \colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $v\det(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^{\times}$.
--
--   **Indefinite quaternion side and the moduli data.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB` the predicate `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and for a finite place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ the algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $v$ lies above $r$ or above $\bar r$. A maximal order $\Lambda$ in $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ (`hΛ`: $\Lambda$ is an order and is maximal among orders containing it). A scheme $\mathcal X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and an assignment `pt` sending a commutative ring $S$, a morphism $s \colon \operatorname{Spec}S \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $S$ of type $(\Lambda, N)$ (an abelian scheme of relative dimension two with commutative relative group law, an action of $\Lambda$ subject to additivity, multiplicativity and a trace condition, and a level-$N$ datum; the clauses of the structure `FakeEllipticCurve` are summarised here) to an $S$-point of $\mathcal X$ over $s$; `h𝒳` asserts that this is a coarse moduli datum (`IsCoarseModuli`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change along ring maps, surjectivity and injectivity on points with values in algebraically closed fields, and the universal property among such functorial assignments). Typeclass hypotheses require the generic fibre — the second projection of the pullback of $f$ along $\operatorname{Spec}K_0 \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ — to be geometrically reduced and geometrically connected.
--
--   An auxiliary level $n \ge 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $\gcd(n,N) = 1$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ via $f_M$ with an assignment `ptF` on pairs consisting of a fake elliptic curve and a full level-$n$ structure on it, and `hM` asserting that this is a fine moduli datum (`IsFineModuli`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, and bijectivity of `ptF` on $S$-points for every $S$). A group $G$ with $\rho \colon G \to \operatorname{Aut}M$ and $\chi \colon G \to \Lambda$, and `hρ` asserting `IsLevelTwistAction` (six clauses: $\rho$ acts over the base; twisting a full level structure by $\chi(g)$ translates the corresponding point by $\rho(g)$; and $\chi$ is, modulo $n$, a multiplicative bijection between $G$ and the invertible classes of $\Lambda/n\Lambda$). A morphism $p \colon M \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`), and compatible with the moduli assignments in the sense that $\mathrm{ptF}(S,s,u)$ followed by $p$ is $\mathrm{pt}(S,s,u_1)$, where $u_1$ is the curve underlying $u$ (`hp_pt`).
--
--   For each prime $\ell \notin \{r,\bar r\}$ (the type `HeckeTower.AwayPrime r rbar`) a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ via $g_\ell$ with an assignment `ptT` on fake elliptic curves equipped with an extra level-$\ell$ datum, and `h𝒴` asserting that each is a coarse moduli datum in the corresponding sense (`IsCoarseModuliT`, the analogue of `IsCoarseModuli` for extra level $\ell$). Two morphisms $d_0(\ell), d_1(\ell) \colon \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) such that composing `ptT` with $d_0(\ell)$ gives the point of the underlying curve (`hd₀`), and composing with $d_1(\ell)$ gives the point of any curve $d$ receiving a level-$\ell$ isogeny from $u$ (`hd₁`): the two degeneracy maps of the Hecke correspondence at $\ell$. Two endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ realising the Atkin–Lehner quotient relations at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`, via `FakeEllipticCurve.IsAtkinLehnerQuotient`).
--
--   **Definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra exactly for $v$ above $\bar r$. Submodules $\Lambda_1, R_1$ with $\Lambda_1$ a maximal order, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$) and $R_1 \le \Lambda_1$. An idelic unit $n_1$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{\mathrm f}$ lying in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` (the set of units lying in the adelic box of $R_1$ whose inverse does not, with $r\,h^{-1}$ in the box and $r^{-1}h$ not), such that $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ (`meetOrder R₁ n₁`) is an Eichler order of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`). An injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0 \colon \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$, and a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$.
--
--   A subgroup $\tilde\Gamma$ (`Γt`) of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ whose elements are exactly those of [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37), the intersection over all places $w \neq v$ of the preimages, under the map to the local units at $w$, of the subgroups generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$. Families $s, s^{\mathrm f}$ indexed by the tower primes, $s_\ell$ a unit of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ and $s^{\mathrm f}_\ell$ an idelic unit, subject to the four clauses of `hs`: at every place $u$ not containing $r$ the $u$-component of $s^{\mathrm f}_\ell$ is $s_\ell \otimes 1$; at every place $u$ containing $r$ it is $1$; the product of the diagonal idele of the scalar $\ell$ with $(s^{\mathrm f}_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise; and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$. Subgroups $\tilde\Gamma_\ell$ (`Γtℓ`) defined by $\tilde\Gamma_\ell = \tilde\Gamma \cap s_\ell \tilde\Gamma s_\ell^{-1}$. A unit $\bar w$ with reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\tilde\Gamma$ (`hwbar`). A group homomorphism $\theta_t \colon \tilde\Gamma \to G$.
--
--   **The uniformisation families.** For every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, write $\mathcal F(B) = \big((Onr \to_{\mathcal O} B) \times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}(\pi, B)\big) \times G$, where a Deligne datum over $B$ assigns to each full $\mathcal O$-lattice $M$ in $K_0^2$ a $B$-submodule of $B \otimes_{\mathcal O} M$ with invertible quotient, monotone under inclusions of lattices, equivariant for homothety, and non-degenerate at every prime of $B$; and write $M(B)$ for the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B \to M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ (`Scheme.nilpPoints`). Given: maps $\Theta_f \colon \mathcal F(B) \to M(B)$ and, for each tower prime, $\Theta_T(\ell)$ from $(Onr \to_{\mathcal O} B) \times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}(\pi,B)$ to $\mathcal Y_\ell(B)$; the hypothesis `hnat` that $\Theta_f$ is natural in $B$; `hG` that for all $g,h \in G$ the map on points induced by $\rho(h)$ carries $\Theta_f(x, gh)$ to $\Theta_f(x,g)$; `hinv` that for $\gamma \in \tilde\Gamma$ and $x, x'$ related by `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` for $\iota_0(\gamma)$ — that is, $x'_1 = x_1 \circ Fr^{-v\det \iota_0(\gamma)}$ and $x'_2$ is the pullback of $x_2$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback` — one has $\Theta_f(x', \theta_t(\gamma)g) = \Theta_f(x,g)$; and `het`, a formal étaleness clause: for a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra map $p \colon B \to B_0$ with $\pi$ nilpotent in both and with $\ker p$ of square zero (stated as: any two elements killed by $p$ have product $0$), every $x_0 \in \mathcal F(B_0)$ and every $y \in M(B)$ lifting $\Theta_f(x_0)$ admit a unique $x \in \mathcal F(B)$ with image $x_0$ and $\Theta_f(x) = y$.
--
--   **Level-$\ell$ data.** A tower prime $\ell$, a scheme $M_\ell$ with a morphism $f_{M_\ell}$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ which is locally of finite type (`hfMℓ`), and maps $\Theta_{f,\ell} \colon \mathcal F(B) \to M_\ell(B)$ satisfying the analogues `hnatℓ` (naturality in $B$) and `hetℓ` (the same formal étaleness clause), and `hinvℓ`, which is the analogue of `hinv` restricted to elements $\gamma$ lying both in $\tilde\Gamma$ and in $\tilde\Gamma_\ell$. No moduli-theoretic hypothesis on $M_\ell$ beyond these is imposed.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, all $x_1, x_2 \in (Onr \to_{\mathcal O} B) \times \mathrm{DeligneDatum}(\pi,B)$ and all $g_1,g_2 \in G$ with $\Theta_{f,\ell}(x_1,g_1) = \Theta_{f,\ell}(x_2,g_2)$, every field $L$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, every $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi \colon B \to L$ and every $\gamma$ lying in $\tilde\Gamma$ and in $\tilde\Gamma_\ell$: if, after base change along $\varphi$, the three relations
--
--   (i) `DeligneDatum.IsPullback` holds for $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ between the Deligne data $\varphi_*(x_1)_2$ and $\varphi_*(x_2)_2$, that is, for every full lattice $M$ the line of $\varphi_*(x_2)_2$ at $M$ is the preimage, under the base-changed action of $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, of the line of $\varphi_*(x_1)_2$ at $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}M$;
--
--   (ii) for every $y \in Onr$ which is fixed by $Fr^{v\det \iota_0(z)}$ for every $z \in \tilde\Gamma$ that is a rational scalar ($z = c \cdot 1$ for some $c \in \mathbb Q$) and satisfies $\theta_t(z) = 1$, one has $\varphi_*(x_2)_1(y) = \big(\varphi_*(x_1)_1 \circ Fr^{-v\det \iota_0(\gamma)}\big)(y)$;
--
--   (iii) $g_2 = \theta_t(\gamma)\,g_1$;
--
--   hold, then there exists $f \in B$ with $\varphi(f) \neq 0$ such that for every $\mathcal O$-algebra $C$ and every $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\chi \colon B \to C$ for which $\chi(f)$ is a unit, the same three relations hold with $\chi$ in place of $\varphi$: $\mathrm{IsPullback}$ for $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$ between $\chi_*(x_1)_2$ and $\chi_*(x_2)_2$; the Frobenius-twist identity $\chi_*(x_2)_1(y) = \big(\chi_*(x_1)_1 \circ Fr^{-v\det \iota_0(\gamma)}\big)(y)$ for all $y \in Onr$ fixed by the same family of Frobenius powers; and $g_2 = \theta_t(\gamma)\,g_1$ (this last conjunct does not involve $\chi$ and is repeated verbatim from the hypothesis).
--
--   In the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to the indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$, two points of the formal model with the same image in the level-$\ell$ lift $M_\ell$ differ, over a field-valued point, by an element $\gamma$ of $\tilde\Gamma \cap \tilde\Gamma_\ell$ acting simultaneously on the Deligne datum, on the unramified coefficient homomorphism by a Frobenius twist, and on the $G$-label; the statement says that this orbit relation, once valid at a field-valued point, remains valid over a Zariski neighbourhood, in the form of an element $f \in B$ invertible on that neighbourhood. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuliT.exists_flat_family_isPullback_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuliT.exists_flat_family_isPullback_of_cerednikDrinfeld_uniformization_fine_eq), which turns this local spreading into a family over a flat base.
